<section class="descriptions">
    <div class="descriptions-row">
        <div class="descriptions-label">
            <h2>Show variable descriptions</h2>
            <p>
                Lists every setting with the sentence explaining what it does. With this off a
                section is its labels and variable names alone, which is shorter to read once the
                settings are familiar.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="descriptions-control">
            @if (IsLoading)
            {
                <span class="control-note">Reading…</span>
            }
            else
            {
                <label class="switch">
                    <input type="checkbox"
                           checked="@Current.ShowVariableDescriptions"
                           disabled="@IsBusy"
                           @onchange="OnToggledAsync"/>
                    <span>@(Current.ShowVariableDescriptions ? "On" : "Off")</span>
                </label>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="explanation">
        The variable name is shown either way, and searching still reads the descriptions whether
        or not they are on screen. A configuration screen already open picks this up the next time
        it is opened.
    </p>

    @if (Message is not null)
    {
        <p class="message is-error">@Message</p>
    }
</section>
